      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-general-2013-p1.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(\\quad 24\\) The smallest two integers that are the product of four primes are \\(2^{4}=16\\) and \\(2^{3} \\cdot 3=24\\). Since 16 is a perfect square and 24 is not, the answer is 24 .",
